From: Johan Hovold <johan@kernel.org>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 16:37:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: core: fix adapter deregistration race
References: bsc#1012628
Patch-mainline: 7.1.4
Git-commit: b1a58ed9eab146b36f41a55db8f5d7ce9fdedf3f

commit b1a58ed9eab146b36f41a55db8f5d7ce9fdedf3f upstream.

Adapters can be looked up by their id using i2c_get_adapter() which
takes a reference to the embedded struct device.

Remove the adapter from the IDR before tearing it down during
deregistration (and on registration failure) to make sure its resources
are not accessed after having been freed (e.g. the device name).

Fixes: 35fc37f81881 ("i2c: Limit core locking to the necessary sections")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org	# 2.6.31
Cc: Jean Delvare <khali@linux-fr.org>
Signed-off-by: Johan Hovold <johan@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Wolfram Sang <wsa+renesas@sang-engineering.com>
Signed-off-by: Greg Kroah-Hartman <gregkh@linuxfoundation.org>
Signed-off-by: Jiri Slaby <jslaby@suse.cz>
---
 drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c b/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c
index 623ab97159bf..8bea9fc6888f 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/i2c-core-base.c
@@ -1586,7 +1586,7 @@ static int i2c_register_adapter(struct i2c_adapter *adap)
 	res = device_add(&adap->dev);
 	if (res) {
 		pr_err("adapter '%s': can't register device (%d)\n", adap->name, res);
-		goto err_remove_debugfs;
+		goto err_replace_id;
 	}
 
 	res = i2c_setup_smbus_alert(adap);
@@ -1613,7 +1613,10 @@ static int i2c_register_adapter(struct i2c_adapter *adap)
 out_reg:
 	i2c_deregister_clients(adap);
 	device_del(&adap->dev);
-err_remove_debugfs:
+err_replace_id:
+	mutex_lock(&core_lock);
+	idr_replace(&i2c_adapter_idr, NULL, adap->nr);
+	mutex_unlock(&core_lock);
 	debugfs_remove_recursive(adap->debugfs);
 err_put_adap:
 	init_completion(&adap->dev_released);
@@ -1802,6 +1805,8 @@ void i2c_del_adapter(struct i2c_adapter *adap)
 	/* First make sure that this adapter was ever added */
 	mutex_lock(&core_lock);
 	found = idr_find(&i2c_adapter_idr, adap->nr);
+	if (found == adap)
+		idr_replace(&i2c_adapter_idr, NULL, adap->nr);
 	mutex_unlock(&core_lock);
 	if (found != adap) {
 		pr_debug("attempting to delete unregistered adapter [%s]\n", adap->name);
-- 
